<title>BELGIUM: Belgium mulling Shanghai Bell stake sale - paper.</title>
<headline>Belgium mulling Shanghai Bell stake sale - paper.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Finance Minister Philippe Maystadt is considering selling the Belgian state's nine percent stake in telecommunications joint venture Shanghai Bell, Belgian newspaper De Standaard said on Monday.</p>
<p>The stake is currently worth 300 million to 400 million Belgian francs, up to three times the original 1983 investment of 123 million francs, the paper said. Maystadt made the suggestion during his current trip to China.</p>
<p>Shanghai Bell, founded by Alcatel Bell, the Belgian unit of Alcatel Alsthom, China's  National Post &amp; Telecom Industry and the Belgian state, made 1995 profit of 3.6 billion francs.</p>
<p>The money from the sale would be used to reduce Belgium's state debt.</p>
